From: STD Team <std@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] STD: add Kconfig SMART_TASK_DISTRIBUTOR

Add SMART_TASK_DISTRIBUTOR behind kernel/Kconfig.preempt with
default y. The shim stays above deadline and never adds a new
scheduling class. Default on keeps single image behavior simple.

Signed-off-by: STD Team <std@kernel.org>
---
 kernel/Kconfig.preempt | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/Kconfig.preempt b/kernel/Kconfig.preempt
index f294dad43..27ccc4a2a 100644
--- a/kernel/Kconfig.preempt
+++ b/kernel/Kconfig.preempt
@@ -197,3 +197,13 @@ config SCHED_CLASS_EXT
 	  For more information:
 	    Documentation/scheduler/sched-ext.rst
 	    https://github.com/sched-ext/scx
+
+config SMART_TASK_DISTRIBUTOR
+	bool "Smart Task Distributor routing shim"
+	default y
+	help
+	  Route tasks above the deadline class without adding a new
+	  scheduling class. Fair tasks prefer housekeeping CPUs and
+	  deadline plus real-time tasks prefer non-housekeeping CPUs.
+	  The shim respects affinity, stays off on small systems and
+	  can be toggled at run time via kernel.std_running.
